@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}

<section class="band hero">
    <h1><span class="accent">Donation</span>Tracker</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        A small ASP.NET Core MVC app that records supporters and the donations
        they make, and keeps a running campaign total.
    </p>
    <a asp-controller="Donations" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-primary">View donations</a>
    <a asp-controller="Supporters" asp-action="Index" class="hero-link">View supporters</a>
</section>

<section class="py-5">
    <h2>What <span class="accent-red">it</span> does</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">
        Every form is validated in the browser and again on the server. A
        donation cannot be dated in the future and must belong to an existing
        supporter.
    </p>

    <div class="row g-3">
        <div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3">
            <div class="card card-body feature-card h-100">
                <div class="feature-icon icon-orange">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="4" /><path d="M4 21c0-4 4-6 8-6s8 2 8 6" /></svg>
                </div>
                <h3>Supporters</h3>
                <p>List, add and edit the people who donate, each with a page of their own donations.</p>
                <a asp-controller="Supporters" asp-action="Index">Open supporters</a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3">
            <div class="card card-body feature-card h-100">
                <div class="feature-icon icon-green">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20s-7-4.4-7-9.5A4 4 0 0 1 12 8a4 4 0 0 1 7 2.5C19 15.6 12 20 12 20z" /></svg>
                </div>
                <h3>Donations</h3>
                <p>A paged list with the campaign total, plus add and edit.</p>
                <a asp-controller="Donations" asp-action="Index">Open donations</a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3">
            <div class="card card-body feature-card h-100">
                <div class="feature-icon icon-teal">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 5l-6 7 6 7M16 5l6 7-6 7" /></svg>
                </div>
                <h3>JSON API</h3>
                <p>The same donations as paged JSON, returned as DTOs and never as database entities.</p>
                <a href="/api/donations">Open GET /api/donations</a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-6 col-lg-3">
            <div class="card card-body feature-card h-100">
                <div class="feature-icon icon-pink">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="9" rx="1.5" /><path d="M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3" /></svg>
                </div>
                <h3>Staff sign-in</h3>
                <p>Anyone can view. Only signed-in staff can add or edit, and every change goes in an audit trail.</p>
                <a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Login">Open staff sign in</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-teal">
    <h2>How it was <span class="accent">built</span></h2>
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-6">
            <ul class="mb-0">
                <li><strong>ASP.NET Core MVC on .NET 10</strong>, with Razor views, tag helpers and Bootstrap.</li>
                <li><strong>Entity Framework Core and SQL Server LocalDB</strong>, with the schema managed by migrations.</li>
                <li><strong>Three layers</strong>: controllers call a service, the service calls a repository, and only the repository uses the database context.</li>
                <li><strong>Business rules in the service</strong>, so they can be unit tested without a database.</li>
                <li><strong>NUnit and Moq</strong> unit tests for the service, and integration tests that run the repository against a real database.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-6">
            <ul class="mb-0">
                <li><strong>Hand-written SQL</strong>: a stored procedure the app calls with a parameter, and a covering index measured before and after with execution plans (402 logical reads down to 4).</li>
                <li><strong>A paged JSON API</strong> that returns DTOs, never the database entities.</li>
                <li><strong>ASP.NET Core Identity</strong> for staff sign-in, with hashed passwords.</li>
                <li><strong>An audit trail</strong> saved in the same transaction as the change it records.</li>
                <li><strong>A CI build</strong> that runs every test on each push.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<p class="mt-4 mb-0">
    The full write-up is in the
    <a href="https://github.com/AJWCTech/donation-tracker-aspnet-mvc/blob/master/docs/DEVELOPMENT.md">development notes</a>,
    and the source is on
    <a href="https://github.com/AJWCTech/donation-tracker-aspnet-mvc">GitHub</a>.
    See also the <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Privacy">privacy policy</a>.
</p>
